# With no ceiling on the wait for a connection, a request past what the pool of
# sixteen can serve queues until its whole budget is gone and is refused anyway.

title: the wait for one of the pool's sixteen connections is unbounded
file: internal/ledgerhttp/ledgerhttp.go
run: go test -count=1 -run TestARequestTheBusyPoolCannotServeIsRefusedAtTheCeiling -v ./internal/ledgerhttp/
--- before
	if p.Acquire <= 0 {
		return p.DB.Conn(ctx)
	}
--- after
	if true {
		return p.DB.Conn(ctx)
	}
